  "content": "<table align=\"center\" border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\">\n<tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\">\n<div>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr>\n<td align=\"left\" style=\"padding-left: 4px; font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\"><p>#​645 — October 29, 2026</p></td>\n<td align=\"right\" style=\"padding-right: 4px; font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\"><p><a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/192169/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B;\" target=\"_blank\">Read on the Web</a></p></td>\n</tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\"></td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; margin: 0; padding: 0;\"><img loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/cpress/image/upload/v1653576619/lgfqinzbdqttwmhvljxb.png\" style=\"line-height: 100%;\" width=\"100%\"/></td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\">\n<a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/192128/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B;\" target=\"_blank\"><img loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/cpress/image/upload/w_1280,e_sharpen:60,q_auto/f0gg9aczxjjc0lxcgr7g.jpg\" style=\"line-height: 100%;\" width=\"640\"/></a>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 500 !important; font-size: 18px !important; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/192128/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"nodejs.org\">Node.js 26 'Lithium' Is Now the Active LTS Line</a></span> — Node.js 26.13.0 promotes Node 26 to long-term support, with updates through April 2029, making it the new line to target for production. Node 24 has moved into maintenance and 22 remains in maintenance until April 2027 – <a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/192129/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B;\" target=\"_blank\">the Node releases page</a> has a neat graph to visualize this.</p>\n<p>Node.js Release Team </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\"><p>💡 Meanwhile, Node 27's <a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/192130/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B; font-weight: 600;\" target=\"_blank\">first alpha</a>, the first release under Node's <a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/192131/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B; font-weight: 600;\" target=\"_blank\">new annual release schedule</a>, is being prepared and should land later today.</p></td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/192127/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B;\" target=\"_blank\"><img height=\"110\" loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/cpress/image/upload/c_limit,w_480,h_480,q_auto/copm/fc046e7d.png\" style=\"padding-top: 12px; padding-left: 12px; line-height: 100%;\" width=\"110\"/></a>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 500 !important; font-size: 18px !important; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/192127/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"master.dev\">Build an Agent that Never Sleeps</a></span> — Most agents stop when you close the chat. Learn to build one that keeps working: it triages incidents, asks your permission before risky fixes, and picks up where it left off after a crash.</p>\n<p>Master.dev <span style=\"margin-left: 4px; font-size: 0.9em; color: #997 !important; padding: 1px 4px;\">sponsor</span></p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 500 !important; font-size: 18px !important; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/192132/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"nodejs.org\">Upgrade Now: Node's October Security Releases Fix a Brotli Flaw</a></span> — Last week's releases (26.12.1, 24.22.1 and 22.23.4) fix ten CVEs, including <a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/192170/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B;\" target=\"_blank\">a flaw in the bundled Brotli decoder</a>, since dubbed <a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/192133/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B;\" target=\"_blank\"><em>Node2Shell</em></a>, that can allow remote code execution if apps decompress malicious Brotli data, such as through <code>node:zlib</code>.</p>\n<p>Node.js Project </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><strong>IN BRIEF:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>🔒 Express <a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/192135/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">explains a body-parser bug</a> where trailing bytes after a gzipped body can let a request crash a process. It's fixed in 2.4.0 and 1.20.9.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>After <a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/192136/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">a TSC vote</a>, Node has merged a new experimental flag to <a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/192137/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">strip types from TypeScript in <code>node_modules</code></a>, but only inside packages marked private, such as monorepo workspaces.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/192138/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">Electron 45</a> is out, moving to Chromium 156, V8 15.6 and Node 24.22. Sandboxed preload scripts lose the <code>Buffer</code> and <code>setImmediate</code> globals, and Electron 42 has now reached its <em>end-of-life</em>.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>GitHub Actions <a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/192139/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">workflow lockfiles are now generally available</a> letting you pin actions and their dependencies in participating workflows.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 500 !important; font-size: 18px !important; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/192140/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"redmonk.com\">The Web Can't Afford a JavaScript Runtime Monoculture</a></span> — With Deno's runtime set to wind down after its team's move to Cloudflare, the field of major server-side runtimes could narrow to Node, Bun and <code>workerd</code>. An analyst draws on IE6, Chromium's dominance and the io.js fork to argue why that might worry us.</p>\n<p>Kate Holterhoff (RedMonk) </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\"><p>💡 Meanwhile, Deno's team says it's <a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/192141/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B; font-weight: 600;\" target=\"_blank\">working on getting Deno into a foundation</a>, and an initial fork, <a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/192142/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B; font-weight: 600;\" target=\"_blank\">Ende</a>, has appeared.</p></td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 500 !important; font-size: 18px !important; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/192143/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"reylo.dev\">Reylo: Import <code>.sql</code> Files into TypeScript with Full Type Inference</a></span> — From the creator of Zod: write queries in plain <code>.sql</code> files and <code>import</code> them into TypeScript, with row and param types inferred from the SQL. No codegen step, but it relies on TypeScript 7.1's <a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/192144/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B;\" target=\"_blank\">new content mappers</a> (now in beta).</p>\n<p>Colin McDonnell </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 500 !important; font-size: 18px !important; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/192145/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"clickhouse.com\">Up to 10x Faster Postgres for I/O-Heavy Workloads</a></span> — Managed Postgres on local NVMe, natively integrated with ClickHouse for real-time analytics.</p>\n<p>ClickHouse Managed Postgres <span style=\"margin-left: 4px; font-size: 0.9em; color: #997 !important; padding: 1px 4px;\">sponsor</span></p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p>📄 <a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/192146/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">Why Parallel Publishes Can Briefly Break npm Installs</a> – Monorepo releases can land before their own dependencies. <cite>Evert Pot (vlt)</cite></p>\n<p>📄 <a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/192147/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\"><code>node:vfs</code>: What Shipped, How It Works, and Its Limits</a> <cite>Matteo Collina (Platformatic)</cite></p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\"></td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\"><p>🛠 Code &amp; Tools</p></td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\">\n<a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/192148/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B;\" target=\"_blank\"><img loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/cpress/image/upload/w_1280,e_sharpen:60,q_auto/yfk5ezruwtf6osle2mkp.jpg\" style=\"line-height: 100%;\" width=\"640\"/></a>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 500 !important; font-size: 18px !important; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/192148/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"github.com\">Dependency Cruiser 18.7: Validate and Visualize Your Dependencies</a></span> — Set rules about what may depend on what (no circular imports, say, or no reaching into another package's internals), check them in CI, and render the results as graphs. There's <a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/192149/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B;\" target=\"_blank\">a page of graphs for real projects</a> like Yarn and React.</p>\n<p>Sander Verweij </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 500 !important; font-size: 18px !important; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/192150/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"github.com\">OpenTelemetry JS 3.0 Released</a></span> — OpenTelemetry's JavaScript SDK now ships dual ESM/CommonJS builds with strict <code>exports</code> maps (so deep imports break), and merges the Node, web and base trace SDKs into a single package.</p>\n<p>OpenTelemetry </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\"><p>💡 Meanwhile, a new repo under the Node.js org, <a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/192151/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B; font-weight: 600;\" target=\"_blank\">microtel</a>, prototypes a minimal OpenTelemetry implementation meant to eventually land in Node itself.</p></td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 500 !important; font-size: 18px !important; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/192152/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"bundle.pipobscure.com\">bundle: Ship a Node App as One Signed File</a></span> — Freezes a Node app and its dependency tree into a signed ZIP that Node 26's experimental virtual file system runs directly, with no <code>npm install</code> needed. Its author wrote several of the core VFS pieces it builds on.</p>\n<p>Philipp Dunkel </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 500 !important; font-size: 18px !important; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/192153/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"gpuix-svelte.stanislav.garden\">gpuix-svelte: Native Desktop Apps from Svelte, No Webview</a></span> — Draws Svelte components natively using <a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/192154/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B;\" target=\"_blank\">GPUI</a>, the GPU-powered UI framework behind Zed, while your code runs in Node or Bun. Experimental, as it relies on Svelte's unreleased custom renderers feature. <a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/192155/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B;\" target=\"_blank\">GitHub repo.</a></p>\n<p>Stanislav Khromov </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 500 !important; font-size: 18px !important; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/192156/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"blog.platformatic.dev\">sqlite-js-stream: Litestream, Rewritten for Node by an AI Agent</a></span> — <a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/192157/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B;\" target=\"_blank\">Litestream</a> continuously streams SQLite's write-ahead log to S3 so a single-file database can be recovered. Platformatic has ported the Go tool to TypeScript running directly on <code>node:sqlite</code>.</p>\n<p>Matteo Collina (Platformatic) </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px;\">\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\"></td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p>📰 Classifieds</p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p>🛒 AI agents are completing purchases for real customers. <a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/192158/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">Fingerprint</a> identifies them so you don’t block a sale. <a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/192158/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">Learn how</a>.</p>\n<p>📄 <a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/192159/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">Invoices in, JSON out</a>. Pull line items, totals, dates and vendor details from invoice PDFs with <a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/192159/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">Foxit's extraction API</a>.</p>\n</td></tr></table>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\"></td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\">\n<a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/192160/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B;\" target=\"_blank\"><img loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/cpress/image/upload/w_1280,e_sharpen:60,q_auto/mzbu4tbh2l2opaj725sv.jpg\" style=\"line-height: 100%;\" width=\"640\"/></a>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/192160/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">Chokidar 6.0</a> – A rewrite of the popular file watching library <em>(above)</em>. v6 confirms changes against the filesystem before emitting events.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/192161/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">Verdaccio 7.0</a> – Lightweight, self-hostable private npm registry and proxy. <a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/192162/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">v7 adds staged publishing and 2FA</a> and requires Node 24+.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/192163/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">AVA 8.2</a> – Long-standing Node test runner. <a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/192164/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">v8.1 can be up to 50% faster</a> on many common workloads while 8.2 rolls out some fixes.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/192165/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">path-to-regexp 9.0</a> – Library that turns paths like <code>/user/:name</code> into regular expressions, as used by Express. <a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/192166/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">Now ESM-only</a>, with a subtle change to how ambiguous segments match.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/192167/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">Directus 12.6</a> – Connect any SQL database and get instant REST and GraphQL APIs, a visual management Studio, and a native MCP server for AI agents.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/192168/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">Croner 11.0</a> – Library to trigger functions or evaluate cron expressions.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\"></td></tr></table>\n</div>\n</td></tr>\n</table>\n",
  "attachments": []
}